  "title": "Interference adds one phase and no relation in three dimensions",
  "subject": "Which signed one-bit edge laws are invariant under the moves of ordered triangulations of three-manifolds",
  "conclusion": "Every signed one-bit edge law with weights in {-1, 0, 1} invariant under the ordered 2-3 and 1-4 moves has a counting support, and up to sign changes it is a counting law, the twisted Dijkgraaf-Witten law (-1)^(x01 x12 x23) on a cocycle support, or a mix of these. No twisted law is symmetric, so signs need the vertex order, as order alone added nothing to counting.",
